# unseated.allow — catalog directories that no dispatcher panel names, and that
# are deliberately kept that way.
#
# Read by verify-catalog.sh C2b (the reverse orphan sweep). C2 walks panel → catalog
# and catches a panel naming a seat that does not exist. C2b walks catalog → panel
# and catches the opposite: a directory nobody dispatches. Neither direction implies
# the other, and until C2b existed the README promised an orphan check that no gate
# performed.
#
# The point of this file is that "inert" must be a decision someone recorded, not a
# state a directory can drift into. A new directory that is neither seated nor listed
# here fails the gate; an entry here whose directory is gone also fails, so the list
# cannot rot into a set of names for things that no longer exist.
#
# Format: one expert ID per line, optional `# reason` trailer. Blank lines and
# whole-line comments ignored.

# Ratified in the v2 expansion, no dispatcher seats them yet. Each is the second
# half of a tension pair with a seat that IS dispatched (see <id>/meta.yaml
# `paired_with`); seating one means adding it to a panel and re-running C6.
evans        # paired_with fowler   — strategic-DDD ↔ emergent-microservices
hickey       # paired_with beck     — fundamental-simplification ↔ incremental-TDD
majors       # paired_with hashimoto — debugging-in-prod ↔ immutable-prevention
sridharan    # paired_with majors   — resilience-skepticism ↔ operational-realism
torvalds     # paired_with ritchie  — Linux pragmatism ↔ Unix purity
unclebob     # paired_with fowler   — principle-purity ↔ economic-pragmatic
lerdorf      # PHP stack; no PHP dispatcher exists
colvin       # Pydantic/MCP; paired_with willison

# Co-Pilot incubation seats — a third stack (python-telegram-bot v20 + FastAPI
# webhook + Firestore + Cloud Run/VPS hybrid) with no dispatcher in this catalog.
# Full disposition in README.md, "Recorded disposition: Co-Pilot incubation seats".
backend-python-ptb
deploy-copilot
firestore-doc
